# `COPY . .` in the build stage, and the final stage copies /app wholesale from
# it. Without this file that meant backend/.env — live SMTP credentials and a
# Firebase service account key — was baked into every locally built image, and
# stayed there in the layer even though nothing in the image reads it.
#
# Render builds from git, where .env is ignored, so the deployed image was never
# affected. Any `docker build` on a developer's machine or in CI was.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Rebuilt inside the image by `uv sync`, and built for the host's platform, so
# copying it in is both a large layer and the wrong binaries.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# History and local scratch have no business in a runtime image.
.git/
.gitignore
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.sqlite3
